# Wave W17-Z (Route 216): pack turf — packed-snow ground, bridge-white, wind-scoured: a hard white pack carrying blue-grey scour flecks and short wind streaks carved across it, the snow the mountain’s north door opens onto (design: wind-scoured snowfields, the drifts carved into waves; the wind here has a long memory and short patience). Route 216’s own snow ground — split from its twin Route 217’s white turf by texture entire (scoured pack vs smooth bench snow) and from Lake Insight’s calm turf by temper: this snow is worked by wind, that one is kept by stillness. Pale, cold, unbroken — the winter form of the ground law.
